 metaDescription:'A step-by-step Learning Path lesson for 2-year-olds: nee-naw to the rescue, run a teddy clinic with a big cuddle at the end, and learn that ambulances help people.',
 intro:'This lesson pairs the siren with the care: the ambulance rushes, the paramedic checks, the teddy gets an examination and a cuddle — empathy practice wearing a siren.',
 what:'An ambulance is a white van with flashing lights that carries helpers to people who need a doctor — and it goes nee-naw, same notes as the fire truck.',
 mean:'Same siren, different job: the ambulance and fire truck make one matching game and one first sorting lesson — two vehicles, one sound, two kinds of helping.',
 know:'Ambulances carry paramedics, whose whole job is helping people feel better. If your toddler ever rides one, the familiar sound and story make a hard day easier.',
 why:'The caring play is the payload here: checking a teddy’s heartbeat, wrapping a blanket, delivering a cuddle. Naming the feeling of being helped is the beginning of empathy.',
